  "notes": "まったり is a mimetic word that evokes a sense of gentle relaxation or smoothness. Originally used in Kansai dialect to describe rich flavors, it expanded nationwide to describe a relaxed lifestyle.\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is casual/colloquial language that became popular in the 1990s-2000s.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- まったりする: to chill out, relax\n- まったり{過|す}ごす: to spend time in a laid-back way\n- まったりした{味|あじ}: mellow/rich taste",
